#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-check-ignore(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:7
msgid "git-check-ignore - Debug gitignore / exclude files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:14
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t'git check-ignore' [<options>] <pathname>...\n"
"\t'git check-ignore' [<options>] --stdin\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:22
msgid ""
"For each pathname given via the command-line or from a file via `--stdin`, "
"check whether the file is excluded by .gitignore (or other input files to "
"the exclude mechanism) and output the path if it is excluded."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:25
msgid ""
"By default, tracked files are not shown at all since they are not subject to "
"exclude rules; but see `--no-index'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-q`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--quiet`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:32
msgid ""
"Don't output anything, just set exit status.  This is only valid with a "
"single pathname."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-v`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--verbose`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:41
msgid ""
"Instead of printing the paths that are excluded, for each path that matches "
"an exclude pattern, print the exclude pattern together with the path.  "
"(Matching an exclude pattern usually means the path is excluded, but if the "
"pattern begins with \"`!`\" then it is a negated pattern and matching it "
"means the path is NOT excluded.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:44
msgid ""
"For precedence rules within and between exclude sources, see "
"linkgit:gitignore[5]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:45
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--stdin`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:48
msgid ""
"Read pathnames from the standard input, one per line, instead of from the "
"command-line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:49
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-z`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:53
msgid ""
"The output format is modified to be machine-parsable (see below).  If "
"`--stdin` is also given, input paths are separated with a NUL character "
"instead of a linefeed character."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-n`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:55
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--non-matching`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:60
msgid ""
"Show given paths which don't match any pattern.  This only makes sense when "
"`--verbose` is enabled, otherwise it would not be possible to distinguish "
"between paths which match a pattern and those which don't."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:61
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-index`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:67
msgid ""
"Don't look in the index when undertaking the checks. This can be used to "
"debug why a path became tracked by e.g. `git add .` and was not ignored by "
"the rules as expected by the user or when developing patterns including "
"negation to match a path previously added with `git add -f`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:69
#, no-wrap
msgid "OUTPUT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:75
msgid ""
"By default, any of the given pathnames which match an ignore pattern will be "
"output, one per line.  If no pattern matches a given path, nothing will be "
"output for that path; this means that path will not be ignored."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:77
msgid "If `--verbose` is specified, the output is a series of lines of the form:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:79
msgid "<source> <COLON> <linenum> <COLON> <pattern> <HT> <pathname>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:87
msgid ""
"<pathname> is the path of a file being queried, <pattern> is the matching "
"pattern, <source> is the pattern's source file, and <linenum> is the line "
"number of the pattern within that source.  If the pattern contained a "
"\"`!`\" prefix or \"`/`\" suffix, it will be preserved in the output.  "
"<source> will be an absolute path when referring to the file configured by "
"`core.excludesFile`, or relative to the repository root when referring to "
"`.git/info/exclude` or a per-directory exclude file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:91
msgid ""
"If `-z` is specified, the pathnames in the output are delimited by the null "
"character; if `--verbose` is also specified then null characters are also "
"used instead of colons and hard tabs:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:93
msgid "<source> <NULL> <linenum> <NULL> <pattern> <NULL> <pathname> <NULL>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:103
msgid ""
"If `-n` or `--non-matching` are specified, non-matching pathnames will also "
"be output, in which case all fields in each output record except for "
"<pathname> will be empty.  This can be useful when running "
"non-interactively, so that files can be incrementally streamed to STDIN of a "
"long-running check-ignore process, and for each of these files, STDOUT will "
"indicate whether that file matched a pattern or not.  (Without this option, "
"it would be impossible to tell whether the absence of output for a given "
"file meant that it didn't match any pattern, or that the output hadn't been "
"generated yet.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-check-ignore.adoc:108
msgid ""
"Buffering happens as documented under the `GIT_FLUSH` option in "
"linkgit:git[1].  The caller is responsible for avoiding deadlocks caused by "
"overfilling an input buffer or reading from an empty output buffer."
msgstr ""

